---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro"
import { TextLink } from "@/components/TextLink"
import {
  archive,
  formatLongDate,
  hasVerifiedPen,
  priceDates,
  tablets,
} from "@/lib/catalog"

const researched = tablets.length + archive.length
const withPen = tablets.filter(hasVerifiedPen).length
const checkedOn = priceDates().at(-1)!
---

<PageLayout
  title="How Tabwise chooses student tablets"
  description="See how Tabwise chooses student tablets using pen compatibility, palm rejection, complete costs and sourced evidence."
  width="max-w-2xl"
>
  <h1 class="page-heading">How we choose tablets</h1>
  <p class="page-intro">
    Tabwise helps students in India find new tablets for notes, PDFs, reading,
    lectures and light typed work, with a pen or without. It is a student subject
    project, built around a curated, sourced catalog.
  </p>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2>Start with the complete cost</h2>
    <p>
      Buying a pen now counts the exact tablet and its named compatible active
      pen together. Buying a pen later checks that same verified setup, but
      shows a separate pen’s dated cost outside today’s tablet budget. If a
      verified pen is already included, the full purchase price still counts.
      Future accessory prices and stock can change.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prices are dated reference observations in INR. They exclude card offers
      and trade-ins, and do not guarantee current stock or delivery to your
      postcode. Check the seller before buying.
    </p>
    <p>
      Without a pen, only the listed tablet purchase is required. An unavoidable
      bundle is still counted in full, never split into invented component
      prices. Tablet-only eligibility does not establish pen compatibility. An
      unspecified bundled accessory or a generic capacitive stylus is not a
      verified handwriting setup.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2>How the finder chooses</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Keep exact new-India configurations with a documented listed purchase
        price. Exclude unavailable and historical-only offers. For a pen now or
        later, also require a named compatible active pen, documented palm
        rejection and a complete setup cost. Unknown or conflicting pen evidence
        can qualify only for a tablet-only purchase.
      </li>
      <li>
        Filter by the appropriate budget, required platform and any relevant
        optional mobile-data, built-in storage and pen-pressure requirements.
        Select the cheapest qualifying configuration per model. Full Windows or
        macOS desktop software is outside this Android/iPadOS catalog.
      </li>
      <li>
        Order the remaining tablets by your screen-space or portability
        preference and main study use, giving the optional secondary use less
        influence. Show up to three distinct models, with lower cost breaking
        ties.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-4">
      A roomy screen means at least 12 inches. A lighter tablet means its listed
      upper weight is at most 525g, excluding the case and pen. PDFs favor
      roomier screens; diagrams also favor documented pen pressure sensitivity.
      Notes favor a verified bundled pen and a lighter tablet. Reading favors
      lower weight; lectures favor screens of at least 11 inches. Typed work
      favors screen space and documented RAM of 8GB or more. These are simple
      preference rules, not claims of measured app performance. Your size
      preference has the strongest priority.
    </p>
    <p>
      If no purchase fits, we show the minimum for the same requirements when
      one exists, or explain that the catalog has no verified match. We never
      silently increase the budget or relax a hard requirement. Size is a soft
      preference: any smaller or heavier fallback is labelled. The finder asks
      five core questions and a sixth essentials question only when relevant;
      editing answers clears hidden follow-up filters.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
    <p>
      Our research covers {researched} models across Apple, Samsung,
      Xiaomi/Redmi, OnePlus, Motorola and Lenovo. {tablets.length} have a
      current documented purchase offer; {withPen} also have a qualifying
      verified pen setup. Manufacturer documentation supplies specifications and
      compatibility; retailers supply dated prices and availability
      observations; independent reviewers supply attributed usage observations.
    </p>
    <p>
      We have not tested the tablets firsthand. A review of one pen, app or
      regional variant does not establish how every other combination behaves.
      Results identify those conditions and link to their sources. Newly added
      models without an independent usage review are explicitly labelled rather
      than given invented review observations. Unknown information stays
      unknown.
    </p>
    <p>
      These are documentation-based preference rules, not trained machine
      learning or objective product-quality scores. Battery capacity alone is
      not treated as measured battery life.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2>What is stored</h2>
    <p>
      The catalog is prepared before publication. Your answers are processed in
      your browser; Tabwise does not save or send them to a server. Theme
      preference is saved on your device. Product images load from manufacturer
      websites, and purchase links open the relevant external seller.
    </p>
    <p>
      The latest research batch was checked on{" "}
      <time datetime={checkedOn}>{formatLongDate(checkedOn)}</time>; individual
      price dates remain visible.{" "}
      <TextLink href="/tablets/">Browse the tablets and source notes</TextLink>,
      or <TextLink href="/">start the finder</TextLink>.
    </p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
